case the page for regs
target none
covers 1
$ man regs
out 1129
NAME
    regs - dump CPU/video/APU registers

SYNOPSIS
    regs
    regs <cpu>

DESCRIPTION
    Prints the current core's CPU registers, video (PPU) registers, and (if
    the core reports any) APU registers, each in their own section. Field
    widths adapt to each register's real bit width.

OTHER PROCESSORS
    'regs <cpu>' prints just one chip's registers - see 'man cpus'. Bare
    'regs' keeps printing every section at once, which stays the right
    default when the question is 'what is the machine doing' rather than
    'what is this one chip doing'.

    The coprocessor section shows the processor 'cop' names (the first after
    the main one that is not the SPC700), so on a core of the stable ABI it
    is that processor's own registers, as 'regs <name>' prints them.

    Every value here is read through a side-effect-free view, never the
    chip's own register window - reading a real coprocessor status register
    can acknowledge an interrupt or advance a transfer handshake, and a
    debugger that did that would change the run it is meant to observe.

SEE ALSO
    cpus, eval, cophist, copflow, watch
status 0
action none
end

case the page for cophist
target none
covers 1
$ man cophist
out 777
NAME
    cophist - coprocessor register history

SYNOPSIS
    cophist [<reg>] [<count>]

DESCRIPTION
    Prints the retained history of the cartridge coprocessor's registers -
    the SuperFX GSU, the SA-1, or a NEC DSP - one row per refresh, oldest
    first. Where `regs` shows the instant, this shows the run-up to it.

    Give <reg> to follow a single register (SFR, PBR, R15, ...) instead of
    the whole file, and <count> to change how many rows are shown from the
    default 16. The header also reports how many refreshes the registers
    have gone unchanged, which is the direct answer to "when did the chip
    stop".

    Prints nothing useful on a cartridge with no coprocessor, which is most
    of them.

EXAMPLES
    cophist
    cophist SFR 64
    cophist R15
status 0
action none
end

