case the page for tile
target none
covers 1
$ man tile
out 875
NAME
    tile - ASCII-decode one 8x8 tile

SYNOPSIS
    tile <space> <addr> <bpp>

DESCRIPTION
    Decodes and prints one 8x8 tile's pixels as an ASCII grid of hex nibbles
    (or '.' for a transparent/zero pixel). <bpp> meaning is core-specific -
    2/4/8 bits-per-pixel on the SNES.

    The decoding is the core's own (IDebugTarget.DecodeTilePixels), since a
    tile's layout is the console's. A core that decodes no tiles answers
    with no pixels, and 'tile' then says so and fails. That is every core
    reached through core ABI v1 today: v1 carries no console views (the
    tiles, sprites and palettes are extensions, EmuSen_CoreAPI.md §6.14),
    so Nephrite and VenusRT refuse here. Until 2026-10-10 the command read
    64 pixels from the empty answer and failed with the platform's
    'Index was outside the bounds of the array'.

EXAMPLES
    tile VRAM 0 4
status 0
action none
end

