case the page for awk
target none
covers 1
$ man awk
out 1103
NAME
    awk - a small AWK subset for reshaping text by field

SYNOPSIS
    awk [-F sep] 'program' [path]

DESCRIPTION
    Real AWK is a whole language; this is deliberately a small subset -
    enough to cover 'filter/reshape another command's output by field',
    without embedding a second full expression language. Supported
    patterns: empty (matches every line), /regex/, NR==N (also !=, <, <=, >,
    >=), BEGIN, END. Supported actions: {print expr[, expr...][; print
    ...]}, where expr is $0, $N, $NF, NR, NF, a "quoted string", or a bare
    number - no concatenation, no arithmetic, no user variables. A bare
    pattern with no {...} defaults to {print $0} (real awk's own default
    action); an explicit empty {} does nothing. Field splitting is
    whitespace-runs by default, or a literal separator string via -F (not a
    regex the way real awk's multi-character -F is). Reads piped stdin, or a
    trailing file path (walled to the project's own directory tree).

EXAMPLES
    regs | awk '{print $1}'
    watch log 1 | awk -F, 'NR>1{print $2}'
    echo -e "a\nb\nc" | awk 'NR==2'
status 0
action none
end

