NAME
    clear - clear the terminal screen

SYNOPSIS
    clear

DESCRIPTION
    Wipes whatever's currently on screen (a real Console.Clear(), not just
    printing blank lines) so the next prompt starts at the top instead of at
    the bottom of a long scrollback. Only does anything against a real
    interactive console; a redirected/nonexistent one (a piped script, a
    'source'd file, a headless test) is silently a no-op rather than an
    error, since there was never a real screen to clear in the first place.

    In EmuSen.Mistress's own console window (a TextBox, not a real
    terminal), 'clear' is replaced with a windowed equivalent instead: it
    empties that window's own output text rather than touching a system
    console that doesn't exist there.

EXAMPLES
    clear
