case the page for su
target none
covers 1
$ man su
out 930
NAME
    su - switch this shell's active account

SYNOPSIS
    su [name]

DESCRIPTION
    Switches THIS shell (this tmux session, if any - see 'tmux') to <name>,
    or back to 'root' with no argument, matching real su's own default
    target. <name> must already exist (see 'useradd'). Does NOT check
    'passwd's stored password hash - nothing in this shell enforces
    anything based on which account is active yet, so su succeeds
    unconditionally for any existing account. That enforcement (e.g. a
    restricted account that can't run mutating commands) is real future
    work, not yet built - this pass is the identity/account plumbing it
    will eventually sit on top of, nothing more.

    A new session created with 'tmux new' inherits whoever created it
    (not always 'root') and a ROM swap preserves each session's own current
    account across the rebuild - see 'tmux'/'core'.

EXAMPLES
    su
    su parent
status 0
action none
end

